# Disruptor of Currents: "return up to one other target nonland permanent to its owner's hand" (CR 603.2, 701.1a). On turn 3 Black Lotus and two Moxen pay
# the five mana; Bot2's Forest (a land) is refused as a target, its Elvish Mystic is accepted and goes back to Bot2's hand, not the controller's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Disruptor of Currents
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Disruptor of Currents.Cast
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Forest)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Power = 1
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest
Bot1.Battlefield.Disruptor of Currents.Tapped = false
